# The frontend talks to the backend through its OWN origin: it calls "/api/..."
# and, in development, the Vite dev server forwards those calls to the backend
# (see vite.config.js). That keeps the API same-origin, which is what lets the
# HttpOnly session cookie work without CORS. So nothing needs to be set here for
# normal development or for a single-origin production deployment.
#
# Only if the backend runs on a port other than 3000 (dev server only, never
# exposed to the browser):
# DEV_API_PROXY_TARGET=http://localhost:3001
#
# Only for a deployment that really serves the API from a DIFFERENT origin than
# the page. It then also needs CORS_ORIGINS and ALLOWED_ORIGINS on the backend,
# and the session cookie must be usable cross-site, which this project's
# SameSite=Strict setting deliberately does not allow — prefer a single origin.
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=
